### Fix 10 (refined): `serve-history.ts` — filter out entries without timestamps

**User direction:** "entries w/o ts should be filtered out"

**Revised plan:** Instead of sorting timestamp-less entries to `MAX_SAFE_INTEGER`, **filter them out entirely** before the sort. This is cleaner — legacy pre-timestamp entries have no reliable chronological position, so including them (even at the end) can confuse the history display.

**BEFORE:**
```ts
combined.sort((a, b) => (a.timestamp ?? 0) - (b.timestamp ?? 0));
```

**AFTER:**
```ts
// Filter out entries without a timestamp — legacy pre-timestamp
// transcript lines have no reliable chronological position.
const timestamped = combined.filter((e) => typeof e.timestamp === 'number');
timestamped.sort((a, b) => (a.timestamp ?? 0) - (b.timestamp ?? 0));
const sorted = timestamped;
```

Then the `MAX_LOG_SIZE` cap uses `sorted` instead of `combined`:
```ts
if (sorted.length > MAX_LOG_SIZE) {
  return sorted.slice(sorted.length - MAX_LOG_SIZE);
}
return sorted;
```

