# Fix Plan: Abort-Listener Cleanup for Stream Timeout Path

## Problem

Three anonymous `'abort'` listeners are registered on a shared `AbortSignal` and never removed on the normal (non-abort) completion path. `{ once: true }` only auto-removes when the signal actually fires `'abort'` — on the normal path (stream completes, timeout resolves, `chatPromise` wins the race), the listener stays attached.

**Accumulation:** Bounded per-`retryChat` call (~3-4 listeners × maxRetries), and GC'd with the per-call `AbortController` after the turn.BUT within a single hint round (`hint-round.ts:200` `while(true)` reuses the same live signal across `retryLoop` retries on malformed JSON), accumulation is **unbounded** — each retry iteration adds ~11 listeners (4 collectStream + 3 sleep + 4 postRace) to the same live signal, reclaimed only when the round ends.

