The slow part of `handleTool` is `loader.execute` (I/O-bound tool execution: bash, web_search, read_file). The post-execution bookkeeping (`triologue.tool`, `sequence.add`, `requestEmbeddingTracker`, confusion index) is fast but **order-dependent** — it must remain sequential to preserve the TP constraint, sequence tracking accuracy, and semantic duplication detection. The plan: **parallel execution, sequential post-processing, gated by a safety classification**.

