### Assumptions

1. **Node.js single-threaded**: `increaseConfusionIndex`, `sequence.add`, and `triologue.tool` are synchronous mutations — safe from data races. The only concurrency is in the async I/O (`loader.execute`, `getEmbedding`).
2. **`escAware` supports concurrent calls**: Each call registers its own `onNeglected` callback in the Set. `triggerNeglection()` iterates all callbacks and clears the Set. Verified in `agent-io.ts`.
3. **`Promise.all` waits for all**: Even if one tool throws, the individual try-catch in each promise prevents `Promise.all` from rejecting early. All results are collected.
4. **LLM rarely issues order-dependent read-only tools**: The safety gate (parallel-safe only) prevents parallelizing order-dependent mutating tools. For read-only tools, order doesn't matter (reading two different files in any order yields the same results).

