### Section 2 — serve-hub.ts: Steering wakes PROMPT

**2a. Modify the `'steer'` case in `onWsMessage`**

```typescript
// BEFORE: always queues
case 'steer':
  if (msg.text) {
    this.pushSteer(msg.text);
  }
  ...
  break;

// AFTER: wakes PROMPT if blocked, otherwise queues
case 'steer':
  if (msg.text) {
    if (this.isInputBlocked()) {
      // Agent is blocked at PROMPT — wake it with the steering text
      // instead of queuing. This handles the race where the frontend's
      // isWaiting hasn't flipped to true yet but the backend is already
      // waiting for input. The steering text becomes the query.
      this.appendUserLog(msg.text, 'steer');
      this.submitInput(msg.text);
    } else {
      this.pushSteer(msg.text);
    }
  }
  if (msg.files && msg.files.length > 0) {
    for (const f of msg.files) {
      this.pushFileUpload({ filename: f.filename, data: f.data, mimeType: f.mimeType, text: msg.text });
    }
  }
  break;
```

**How it works:**
- `isInputBlocked()` returns `true` when `inputResolver` is set (agent at PROMPT, blocked on `waitForInput()`).
- `submitInput(msg.text)` resolves the `inputResolver` with the steering text → `waitForInput()` returns → `prompt.ts` receives it as the query → agent wakes and processes.
- The steering text is logged to `userLog` (persists as a right-side bubble on refresh) but NOT pushed to `steeringQueue` (no 'steer-echo' broadcast — the text goes straight to the agent, not to the buffer bar).
- When the agent is NOT at PROMPT (running, WAIT/auto mode), `isInputBlocked()` is false → `pushSteer()` queues as before → drained at COLLECT as REMINDER or synthesized at next PROMPT.

**No changes needed in `prompt.ts`:** when the PROMPT is woken by steering, `drainSteering()` returns empty (nothing was queued), `synthesizeWithSteering()` is a no-op, and the steering text becomes `triologue.user(query)`. The existing flow handles this cleanly.

