```typescript
async function reloadLead(
  serveActive: boolean,
  servePort: number,
  serveHost: string | null
): Promise<void> {
  isRestarting = true;
  const previousLead = lead;

  // Remember serve state for the new lead
  const wasServeActive = serveMode;
  const rememberedServePort = servePort;
  const rememberedServeHost = serveHost;

  // Reset serveMode — the old lead's ServeHub will be torn down
  serveMode = false;

  // Gracefully shut down serve on the old lead before killing it
  // (same pattern as restart(): on Windows, SIGTERM → TerminateProcess
  // doesn't run signal handlers, so we must IPC-ask the lead to stop Vite)
  if (previousLead) {
    if (wasServeActive || serveActive) {
      let shutdownDone = false;
      const onShutdownDone = (msg: CoordinatorMessage) => {
        if (msg.type === 'serve_shutdown_done') shutdownDone = true;
      };
      previousLead.on('message', onShutdownDone);
      previousLead.send({ type: 'serve_shutdown' });
      await new Promise<void>((resolve) => {
        const deadline = setTimeout(() => resolve(), 1500);
        const check = setInterval(() => {
          if (shutdownDone || previousLead.killed) {
            clearTimeout(deadline);
            clearInterval(check);
            resolve();
          }
        }, 50);
      });
      previousLead.off('message', onShutdownDone);
    }
    previousLead.kill('SIGTERM');
    previousLead.unref();
  }

  // Build args for the new lead:
  // - NO --from flag (fresh session, no context pre-population)
  // - If serve was active, pass --serve <port> so the new lead re-activates
  //   the webui on the same port
  const reloadArgs: string[] = [];
  if (serveActive && rememberedServePort > 0) {
    reloadArgs.push('--serve', String(rememberedServePort));
  }
  if (serveActive && rememberedServeHost) {
    reloadArgs.push('--host', rememberedServeHost);
  }

  const currentLead = startLead(reloadArgs);
  lead = currentLead;

  // Wait for ready signal (same pattern as restart())
  let settled = false;
  await new Promise<void>((resolve) => {
    const onReady = (msg: CoordinatorMessage) => {
      if (msg.type === 'ready' && !settled) {
        settled = true;
        currentLead.off('message', onReady);
        currentLead.off('exit', onFail);
        resolve();
      }
    };
    const onFail = (_code: number | null) => {
      if (!settled) {
        settled = true;
        currentLead.off('message', onReady);
        console.error(chalk.red('New lead process exited unexpectedly during reload.'));
        process.exit(1);
      }
    };
    currentLead.on('message', onReady);
    currentLead.on('exit', onFail);
  });

  isRestarting = false;
}
```

**Key design decisions:**
- **No `--from` flag** → `initializeSession()` sees no session arg → calls `createNewSession()` → fresh empty triologue, no context pre-population. ✅
- **Coordinator is reused** — only the lead process is killed and respawned. Teammates are child processes of the lead; when the lead dies, they are naturally killed. ✅
- **Serve continuity** — the coordinator passes `--serve <port> --host <host>` to the new lead. In `agent-repl.ts` line 534, `shouldServe()` returns true, `getServePort()` returns the port, so `activateServe(port, host)` re-binds the same port. The browser's WebSocket `onclose` handler triggers a reconnect timer (confirmed in `main.ts`), so from the user's perspective the webui disconnects briefly then reconnects with a cleared context. ✅
- **Graceful Vite shutdown** — reuses the same IPC `serve_shutdown` → `serve_shutdown_done` handshake pattern as the existing `restart()` function, critical on Windows where `SIGTERM` calls `TerminateProcess` and signal handlers don't run.
- The function closely mirrors the existing `restart()` function's structure for consistency.

